   "difficulty": 4,
   "stem_html": "<p>f(<span class=\"math\">x</span>) = <span class=\"rt\">√<span class=\"ov\"><span class=\"math\">x</span></span></span> for <span class=\"math\">x</span> ≥ 0, and g(<span class=\"math\">x</span>) = <span class=\"math\">x</span><sup>2</sup> − 4.</p><p>How many real values of <span class=\"math\">x</span> satisfy g(f(<span class=\"math\">x</span>)) = f(g(<span class=\"math\">x</span>)) ?</p>",
   "diagram_svg": null,
   "options": {
    "A": "0",
    "B": "1",
    "C": "2",
    "D": "3",
    "E": "4"
   },
   "answer": "A",
   "solution_html": "<p>g(f(<span class=\"math\">x</span>)) = <span class=\"math\">x</span> − 4 for <span class=\"math\">x</span> ≥ 0. f(g(<span class=\"math\">x</span>)) = <span class=\"rt\">√<span class=\"ov\"><span class=\"math\">x</span><sup>2</sup> − 4</span></span>, defined for |<span class=\"math\">x</span>| ≥ 2.</p><p>Need <span class=\"math\">x</span> − 4 = <span class=\"rt\">√<span class=\"ov\"><span class=\"math\">x</span><sup>2</sup> − 4</span></span>. The right side is ≥ 0, so <span class=\"math\">x</span> ≥ 4. Squaring: <span class=\"math\">x</span><sup>2</sup> − 8<span class=\"math\">x</span> + 16 = <span class=\"math\">x</span><sup>2</sup> − 4, so <span class=\"math\">x</span> = 5/2.</p><p>But 5/2 &lt; 4, so it fails the sign condition (and indeed 5/2 − 4 &lt; 0 while the square root is positive). <span class=\"key\">No solutions</span>.</p>",
   "traps": {
    "B": "x = 5/2 comes from squaring without checking that x − 4 must be non-negative.",
    "C": "Counting ±5/2; neither works.",
    "D": "No route.",
    "E": "No route."
   },
   "detail": "Composite functions & domains"
