   "difficulty": 3,
   "stem_html": "<p>A convergent geometric series has sum to infinity equal to 3 times its first term.</p><p>The odd-numbered terms (1st, 3rd, 5th, …) form another geometric series. The sum to infinity of this new series, as a fraction of the sum to infinity of the original series, is</p>",
   "diagram_svg": null,
   "options": {
    "A": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>1</span><span>3</span></span>",
    "B": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>3</span><span>5</span></span>",
    "C": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>1</span><span>2</span></span>",
    "D": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>2</span><span>3</span></span>",
    "E": "<span class=\"fr\"><span>9</span><span>5</span></span>"
   },
   "answer": "B",
   "solution_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">a</span>/(1 − <span class=\"math\">r</span>) = 3<span class=\"math\">a</span> gives <span class=\"math\">r</span> = 2/3.</p><p>Odd-numbered terms: first term <span class=\"math\">a</span>, ratio <span class=\"math\">r</span><sup>2</sup> = 4/9, sum <span class=\"math\">a</span>/(1 − 4/9) = 9<span class=\"math\">a</span>/5.</p><p>Fraction = (9<span class=\"math\">a</span>/5) / (3<span class=\"math\">a</span>) = <span class=\"key\">3/5</span>.</p>",
   "traps": {
    "A": "1/3 is 1 − r, not the required ratio.",
    "C": "Assumes the odd terms are exactly half the total; they are more than half because they start first.",
    "D": "2/3 is the common ratio.",
    "E": "9/5 is the odd-term sum divided by a, not by the original sum."
   },
   "detail": "Geometric series"
  },
