   "answer": "B",
   "solution_html": "<p>Divide by 9<sup><span class=\"math\">x</span></sup>: (4/9)<sup><span class=\"math\">x</span></sup> + (6/9)<sup><span class=\"math\">x</span></sup> − 2 = 0. With <span class=\"math\">u</span> = (2/3)<sup><span class=\"math\">x</span></sup> this is <span class=\"math\">u</span><sup>2</sup> + <span class=\"math\">u</span> − 2 = 0, so (<span class=\"math\">u</span> + 2)(<span class=\"math\">u</span> − 1) = 0.</p><p><span class=\"math\">u</span> = −2 is impossible (a positive base to a real power is positive). <span class=\"math\">u</span> = 1 gives <span class=\"math\">x</span> = 0.</p><p><span class=\"key\">Exactly one</span> solution.</p>",
